  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building effective and equitable multi-stakeholder mitigation for HWC in Tsavo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will build the capacity and capability of all stakeholders in the landscape to tackle HWC collectively. It will strengthen protected area management&#x2019;s ability to engage communities, especially women and marginalised groups, in participatory, equitable ways, and will facilitate the co-development of solutions to HWC, helping deliver Kenya Wildlife Service&#x2019;s Strategic Plan 2019-2024. This project seeks to build the capacity of KWS-Tsavo to reduce community grievances regarding KWS and protected areas, resulting from HWC, through improving KWS-community collaboration, decision-making processes and governance structures, guided by international best practice, including IUCN Guidelines for HWC</narrative>
  </description>
